section between roadways'. Over, across and within are all an overlap of the footprint with the divider region; no distance stands in for it."},{"span":"f","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.median_or_divider"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.median_or_divider carries an 'opening attribute where a crossover exists': 'through an opening' is the footprint overlapping a divider region of h that carries the opening attribute."},{"span":"g","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.median_or_divider","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"A crossover is a divider region with the opening attribute; an intersection is st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'; rel.occupies places the subject at it. 'Established by a public authority' is a legal status read through the feature's presence."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"At every observation at which the subject occupies a highway h (st.highway) on which a median_or_divider region lies (st.on_way), except where the subject's footprint overlaps an intersection lying on h.","obligation":"Re-binding h as in the applicability: for every median_or_divider region m lying on h, the subject's footprint does not overlap m (rel.occupies), unless m carries the opening attribute (an opening in the divider or a crossover).","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"b","why":"'driven' is read through the vehicle's motion on the highway, whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"g","why":"'established by a public authority' is a legal status; the crossover or intersection present on the road is its evidence.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A st.median_or_divider m without the opening attribute lies on highway h; the subject's footprint overlaps m 